				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Disable telemetry collection by default in build script\n\nUpdate the default values in build.rs for telemetry-related environment variables (`Report`, `OTLPEnabled`, `Capture`). Change the defaults from \"true\" to \"false\" to ensure no telemetry data is captured or sent unless explicitly enabled via environment configuration.\n\nThis aligns the default build behavior with privacy best practices for development and distribution, requiring an explicit opt-in for PostHog, OTLP, and trace capture mechanisms.",
			"SHA": "9cdc391367fd3acde2f55bdac84728cbe413d47a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T16:59:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Initialize native keyring store in main entry\n\nThe SecretProvider requires an initialized keyring store to function correctly for credential retrieval. Previously, the default store was not explicitly set before the first access attempt, causing 'No default store has been set' errors. This failure prevented extensions (such as Roo Code) from completing webview initialization.\n\nAdd an explicit call to `keyring::use_native_store(false)` at the start of the `Fn()` entry point in Source/Binary/Main/Entry.rs. This ensures the native Keychain store on macOS (and Keyutils on Linux) is ready before any secret lookups occur. Implement error logging to track initialization status while allowing graceful fallback if the store setup fails.\n\nThis resolves the startup block for extensions relying on SecretProvider and ensures the boot lifecycle properly configures the system secret management path.",
			"SHA": "1d492cacdf4604910e7c66a9243d23d3dc525682"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T16:14:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix: correct casing for gRPC in comments and default values\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "9932b820dbae0c3f2173a2e07198073acb36001d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T14:09:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Ignore create-dmg support templates in build artifacts\n\nUpdate .gitignore to exclude the `/Target/debug/bundle/share/` and `/Target/release/bundle/share/` directories. These paths contain support templates generated by create-dmg during the macOS bundling process, which are build artifacts and should not be tracked.\n\nThis prevents unnecessary noise in the repository from transient dmg scaffolding files.",
			"SHA": "ceee7047b2f0db6d7f1a82c0330580564b167607"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T14:00:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				24
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Standardize documentation formatting across Environment providers\n\nUpdate doc comments in ConfigurationProvider, DebugProvider, DiagnosticProvider, DocumentProvider, FileSystemProvider, SearchProvider, SourceControlManagementProvider, StorageProvider, TerminalProvider, UserInterfaceProvider, WebviewProvider, and WorkspaceProvider.\n\nChanges include:\n- Replaced em-dashes (—) with hyphens (-) in list items for consistent ASCII formatting.\n- Standardized list indentation and structure across all provider modules.\n- Clarified architectural descriptions and lifecycle steps in Debug, Terminal, and SCM providers.\n- Updated comments in StatusBar.rs to clarify ID validation logic.\n- Removed generated build artifacts from Target/ directories.\n\nThis ensures consistent documentation style across the Mountain backend codebase.",
			"SHA": "c961dae78d35811db8f912f1f9193f04b602fc5f"
		}
	],
